                <pb facs="0584" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg490"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/3043: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ramer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-03-22T11:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">March 22,
                                1924—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:35
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>44. The Department’s 30 March 18, 7 p.m. A note from Nicaraguan Government states
                    that it not only does not object to the use of marines at Chinandega but at this
                    time expresses its consent to similar action in any other analogous case.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
